"The Archaeological Museum of Volos, also known as Athanasakeion Archaeological Museum of Volos, is an archaeology museum in Volos, Greece, that houses many exquisite finds from early 20th-century and modern archaeological excavations in Thessaly. One of the oldest museums of Greece, it was constructed in 1909 and is housed in a neoclassical building.","wpu":"Archaeological Museum of Volos","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/42/Archaeological_Museum_of_Volos.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Museum of Folk Art and History of Pelion","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":39.401649,"lo":22.987008,"d":5872,"ds":"The Museum of Folk Art and History of Pelion (Greek: Μουσείο Λαϊκής Τέχνης και Ιστορίας του Πηλίου) is a museum in the village of Makrinitsa (Volos), Magnesia, Greece. It is housed in the Topali Mansion (Greek: Αρχοντικό Τοπάλη), an 1844 building designated a \"Work of Art and Historical Preserved Monument\".","wpu":"Museum of Folk Art and History of Pelion","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/%CE%91%CF%81%CF%87%CE%BF%CE%BD%CF%84%CE%B9%CE%BA%CF%8C_%CE%A4%CE%BF%CF%80%CE%AC%CE%BB%CE%B7_3888.jpg/960px-%CE%91%CF%81%CF%87%CE%BF%CE%BD%CF%84%CE%B9%CE%BA%CF%8C_%CE%A4%CE%BF%CF%80%CE%AC%CE%BB%CE%B7_3888.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"}],"about":{"ds":"Volos (; Greek: Βόλος [ˈvolos]) is a coastal port city in Thessaly situated midway on the Greek mainland, about 170 kilometres (106 miles) north of Athens and 140 kilometres (87 miles) south of Thessaloniki. It is the capital of the Magnesia regional unit of the Thessaly Region. Volos is also the only outlet to the sea from Thessaly, the country's largest agricultural region.","wpu":"Volos","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/VOLOS-GREECE_-_panoramio_%281%29.jpg/960px-VOLOS-GREECE_-_panoramio_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},"wk":"2026-10-18"}